//   php diy_tool calc     JOBS OUTPUT           material calculators: paint litres, flooring or tile count, concrete volume, lumber lengths (cutting plan)
//   php diy_tool estimate ITEMS OUTPUT [contingency=10 tax=0]   a job estimate sheet: parts, labour and contingency totalled, with problem lines
//   php diy_tool schedule TASKS OUTPUT [today=2026-03-01 within=30]   maintenance schedule: next due dates from last done + interval; overdue and coming up
//
// JOBS is a text file, one job per line (blank lines and # comments are skipped), written  kind: key=value key=value ...
//   paint: room=4x3x2.5 doors=2 windows=1 coats=2 coverage=10 ceiling=yes     room = length x width x height in metres (or walls=24 for the wall area in m2); coverage = m2 per litre, default 10 (read it from the tin)
//   floor: area=12 waste=10 piece=30x30 pack=11                               area in m2 (or room=4x3); piece size in cm (suffix mm, cm, m, in, ft allowed); pack = pieces per box; waste % default 10
//   concrete: length=3 width=2 depth=10cm waste=5 bag=0.0125                  metres unless a suffix; bag = m3 of concrete one bag makes (from the bag: not assumed); waste % default 5
//   lumber: need=2.4,1.8,1.8,0.6 stock=2.4,3.0 kerf=3                         lengths needed and the stock lengths you could buy, in metres (or with a suffix); kerf = saw cut in mm; a cutting plan per stock length
// ITEMS is a CSV: item, type (part or labour, in several languages), quantity (or hours), unit price (or hourly rate). TASKS is a CSV: task, last done (date), interval (6 months, 1 year, 90 days, 2 weeks).
// Quantities are estimates from the numbers you give; read the product's own coverage and yield and buy a margin. SAFETY: electrical, gas, structural, roof, chimney, asbestos and similar work belongs to
// licensed professionals: this tool only does arithmetic and flags such words. The original is never changed.
// =============================================================================
